sn22.4:4.2 | S: the perception element … | T: the perception element …
sn22.4:4.3 | S: the choices element … | T: the volitional formations element …
sn22.4:4.4 | S: the consciousness element; any attraction, grasping, mental fixation, insistence, and underlying tendencies. With the ending, fading away, cessation, giving away, and letting go of that, the mind is said to be ‘well freed’. | T: the consciousness element, the mind is said to be well liberated.
sn22.4:5.1 | S: So, householder, that’s how to understand the detailed meaning of what the Buddha said in brief in ‘The Questions of Sakka’: | T: “Thus, householder, when it was said by the Blessed One in ‘The Questions of Sakka’:
sn22.4:5.2 | S: ‘Those ascetics and brahmins who are freed due to the ending of craving have reached the ultimate goal, the ultimate sanctuary from the yoke, the ultimate spiritual life, the ultimate end, and are best among gods and humans.’” | T: ‘Those ascetics and brahmins who are liberated in the extinction of craving are those who have reached the ultimate end, the ultimate security from bondage, the ultimate holy life, the ultimate goal, and are best among devas and humans’—
